<header><p class="enc-kicker">Religion / idea · religion</p><h1 class="enc-title">Taoism</h1><p class="enc-meta">Also known as Taoist</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Taoism, or Daoism, is a Chinese philosophical and religious tradition centred on the Dao, or Way, and associated with texts such as the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/daodejing">Daodejing</a>. In the early <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/han-dynasty">Han Dynasty</a>, Taoist-influenced ideas of minimal government shaped imperial policy. The <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/yellow-turban-rebellion">Yellow Turban Rebellion</a> of 184 CE was a millenarian Taoist movement that contributed to the dynasty's decline.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/taoism.jpg" alt="Taoism" width="320" height="203" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: liuzr99 · CC BY-SA 2.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:%E6%AD%A6%E5%BD%93%E5%B1%B1%E7%B4%AB%E9%9C%84%E5%AE%AB_(14739990839).jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
